  "note": "Patcher matrix for B196, BUILT FROM main AT 0a93dc0 (PR #375), seeded from the B195 matrix. ONE owner-requested change over B195: the autonomous weight of the Ping-Pong Table is raised from 450 to 3000, matching the Pool Table it is cloned from. Ping-pong was ALREADY autonomous -- VF2EnableAutonomousCandidates clones the Pool Table's behaviour 0x099 into 0x0B8 and gates it on the table's own object 0x9A -- but at 450 against the Pool Table's default 3000 it was offered about a seventh as often, which read in play as villagers ignoring it. Only the weight moves; the object prerequisite is untouched, so the candidate is still offered ONLY while a ping-pong table is placed. Both variants are covered: the built Assets show PingPongTableStd and InvisiblePingPongTable each declaring object 0x9A on ten cells, and neither carries the stock Pool Table's 0x36. See docs/B196-release-notes.md, which must not disagree with this field.",
